    "body": "Thank you for the issue — and for fixing it in the same breath. The report is precise about the mechanism (definitions landing in a later streamed batch than the caller), which is what made #375 straightforward to review against.\n\nTracked by **#375**, which is open with review comments. It carries `Fixes #374`, so this will close automatically when that lands.\n\nThe change itself is correct — the index construction mirrors `resolveEdges`' in-batch path exactly, so cross-batch and in-batch resolution agree on `dstQualifiedKey`. My open question is cost, not correctness: the prescan parses synchronously on the main thread while the streaming loop uses a worker pool, so every unchanged JS/TS file is re-read and re-parsed on each incremental `ix map`. Details and measurements are on the PR.\n",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/ix-infrastructure/Ix/issues/374#issuecomment-5245018584",
